  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade unions represent and promote workers&apos; interests, with education at the heart of their efforts in Africa, supporting decolonisation and resisting neo-liberal policies. Technological advances and climate change pose new challenges. The ILO&apos;s Abidjan Declaration emphasises decent work, skills development and social dialogue. The ITUC Africa&apos;s TULDA programme aims to build a regional cadre of trade unionists to defend workers&apos; rights and propose alternatives to neo-liberal policies.</narrative>
  </description>
